    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 190,
      "versionNonce": 665397958,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "rMr9q4XOaxn20-R8HeKHc",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1392.6310829262075,
      "y": 1785.5511662982958,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 2690.625,
      "height": 537.6,
      "seed": 1350507910,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788718705729,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "How would you ensure secure authentication for merchants using the payment system?\n- API key management with request signing. Each merchant gets both a public API key for identification and a private secret key for generating time-bound signatures\n- When our API Gateway receives a request, it verifies the signature using the merchant's stored public key, \nvalidates that the timestamp is within an acceptable window (typically 5-15 minutes), and ensures the nonce hasn't been used before\n\nHow would you secure customer credit card information while in transit?\n- client-side encryption. Our JavaScript SDK immediately encrypts card details using our public key before data leaves the customer's browser\n- our servers have private keys stored in Hardware Security Modules (HSMs) to decrypt it\n\nHow would you ensure that no transaction data is ever lost and maintain complete auditability for compliance?\n- audit durability comes from an immutable event stream populated via Change Data Capture (CDC). We are saving everything to s3 permanently\n\nhow to ensure transaction safety & integrity in an Asynchrnous environment?\n- A dedicated reconciliation service consumes timeout events and proactively queries\n payment networks to determine what actually happened. \nExternal events from payment networks also flow through the same event stream, allowing correlation with our internal attempts. ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How would you ensure secure authentication for merchants using the payment system?\n- API key management with request signing. Each merchant gets both a public API key for identification and a private secret key for generating time-bound signatures\n- When our API Gateway receives a request, it verifies the signature using the merchant's stored public key, \nvalidates that the timestamp is within an acceptable window (typically 5-15 minutes), and ensures the nonce hasn't been used before\n\nHow would you secure customer credit card information while in transit?\n- client-side encryption. Our JavaScript SDK immediately encrypts card details using our public key before data leaves the customer's browser\n- our servers have private keys stored in Hardware Security Modules (HSMs) to decrypt it\n\nHow would you ensure that no transaction data is ever lost and maintain complete auditability for compliance?\n- audit durability comes from an immutable event stream populated via Change Data Capture (CDC). We are saving everything to s3 permanently\n\nhow to ensure transaction safety & integrity in an Asynchrnous environment?\n- A dedicated reconciliation service consumes timeout events and proactively queries\n payment networks to determine what actually happened. \nExternal events from payment networks also flow through the same event stream, allowing correlation with our internal attempts. ",
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "baseline": 531
    },
    {
